# Engine keys for Hostinger

Optional. Without keys, sign the engine CLIs in interactively instead (see
[README.md](README.md#engines-and-bots)); with them, bots work as soon as the
install finishes.

```sh
sudo install -d -m 700 /etc/mausbot
sudo cp deploy/hostinger/hostinger.env.example /etc/mausbot/hostinger.env
sudo chmod 600 /etc/mausbot/hostinger.env
sudo nano /etc/mausbot/hostinger.env        # fill the keys you have
sudo sh deploy/hostinger/install.sh --bots-only --domain maus.example.com
```

`install.sh` reads `/etc/mausbot/hostinger.env` by default (`--keys-file`
picks another file). Keys are handed to `openmausbot engine set`, never printed
and never written to the repository.

| Variable | Engine | What it runs |
|---|---|---|
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | `claude` | Claude bots on the API key |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | `openai` | OpenAI API bots |
| `XAI_API_KEY` | `xai` | Grok API bots |
| `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | `openrouter` | OpenRouter models |
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | `groq` | Groq |
| `MISTRAL_API_KEY` | `mistral` | Mistral |
| `CEREBRAS_API_KEY` | `cerebras` | Cerebras |
| `GREENFERENCE_API_KEY` | `greenference` | Greenference |
| `MODELGO_API_KEY` | `modelgo` | ModelGo |

The Claude Code, Codex and Grok CLI engines do not use these keys: sign them
in once on the server, which keeps the login on the data volume.
